1
00:03:31,111 --> 00:03:37,111
Meet the little voices inside your head.

2
00:07:02,222 --> 00:07:08,222
Inside Out is a animation, family, adventure film directed by Pete Docter.

3
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:39,333
When 11-year-old Riley moves to a new city, her Emotions
team up to help her through the transition.

4
00:14:04,444 --> 00:14:10,444
Joy, Fear, Anger, Disgust and Sadness work together, but when Joy and Sadness get
lost, they must journey through unfamiliar places to get back home.

5
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:41,555
Joy (voice), played by Amy Poehler.

6
00:21:06,666 --> 00:21:12,666
Sadness (voice), played by Phyllis Smith.

7
00:24:37,777 --> 00:24:43,777
Bing Bong (voice), played by Richard Kind.

8
00:28:08,888 --> 00:28:14,888
Fear (voice), played by Bill Hader.

9
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Anger (voice), played by Lewis Black.

10
00:35:11,111 --> 00:35:17,111
Disgust (voice), played by Mindy Kaling.

11
00:38:42,222 --> 00:38:48,222
Inside Out is a 2015 American animated coming-of-age film directed by Pete
Docter who co-wrote it with Meg LeFauve and Josh Cooley.

12
00:42:13,333 --> 00:42:19,333
Produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures, the film stars the voices of Amy Poehler, Phyllis Smith,
Richard Kind, Bill Hader, Lewis Black, Mindy Kaling, Kaitlyn Dias, Diane Lane, and Kyle MacLachlan.

13
00:45:44,444 --> 00:45:50,444
Inside Out follows the inner workings of the mind of Riley, a young girl who adapts to her
family's relocation as five personified emotions administer her thoughts and actions.

14
00:49:15,555 --> 00:49:21,555
Docter conceived Inside Out in October 2009 after observing changes
in his daughter's personality as she grew older.

15
00:52:46,666 --> 00:52:52,666
The project was subsequently green-lit, and Docter and co-director Ronnie del Carmen developed the story,
while consulting psychologists and neuroscientists in an effort to accurately portray the mind.

16
00:56:17,777 --> 00:56:23,777
Development took five-and-a-half years on a
budget of approximately $175 million.

17
00:59:48,888 --> 00:59:54,888
Significant changes to the film's story and characters
delayed the film's production schedule.

18
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Inside Out debuted at the 68th Cannes Film Festival on May 18, 2015,
and was released in the United States on June 19.

19
01:06:51,111 --> 01:06:57,111
It received critical acclaim for its craftsmanship, screenplay, subject matter, plot, and vocal
performances—particularly those of Poehler, Smith, Kind, Hader, Kaling, and Black.

20
01:10:22,222 --> 01:10:28,222
The National Board of Review and the American Film Institute
named Inside Out one of the top-ten films of 2015.

21
01:13:53,333 --> 01:13:59,333
It grossed $858.8 million worldwide, finishing its theatrical
run as the seventh-highest-grossing film of 2015.

22
01:17:24,444 --> 01:17:30,444
The film was nominated for two awards at the 88th Academy Awards, winning
Best Animated Feature, and received numerous other accolades.

23
01:20:55,555 --> 01:21:01,555
Philosophical journal Film and Philosophy recognized Inside Out
as one of the best animated films ever made.

24
01:24:26,666 --> 01:24:32,666
A sequel, Inside Out 2, was released in 2024.

25
01:27:57,777 --> 01:28:03,777
The film explores themes of dreams, san francisco,
california, minnesota, sadness, cartoon.

26
01:31:28,888 --> 01:31:34,888
The tone is lighthearted and uplifting and emotional.
